bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    wm_scene_css_render_perf, 0, "Doc OPEN medium, workaround is the pixel cap; wm_scene.spl present"
    wm_scene_css_render_perf, 1, "Optimized src/os/compositor/wm_scene.spl: (1) render_scene_to_backend uses lightweight WebRenderRequest.html().with_pixel_output() avoiding redundant active-theme CSS assembly; (2) _scene_to_html_with_options(scene, false) prunes unused widget CSS selectors and @keyframes/@media motion rules on static pixel renders while keeping scene_to_html() byte-identical; (3) added bounded 16-entry LRU _wm_scene_pixel_cache_* with length-prefixed _wm_scene_cache_field keys avoiding delimiter collisions and repeated CSS/direct renders on identical scenes (80x60 CSS repeat 15113250us->789us vs 26490685us cold baseline, 100x100 CSS repeat 26809313us->888us with exact baseline FNV-1a hashes 14432758499751269943 and 8367153169614613988); (4) eliminated per-row whole-buffer Arc cloning in wm_scene_direct_rect_pixels via _wm_scene_fill_row_span(mut pixels: [u32], ...) / pixels.write_span and added exact frosted IIR steady-state span recovery, cutting 320x200 glass 11946536us->579469us, 320x200 std 3201747us->162441us, 800x600 std 22227960us->803635us (repeat 7532us), 800x600 glass 30870575us->1631080us with 0 pixel diffs vs scalar oracle including sub-16px spans. Verified 5/5 in test/01_unit/os/compositor/wm_scene_css_render_perf_spec.spl and 9/9 in test/01_unit/os/compositor/wm_unified_renderer_spec.spl. WM_SCENE_CSS_RENDER_PIXEL_CAP=10000 remains gated pending Metal verification and upstream browser_engine cold CSS cost."

